line	<col=000080>Heat the preform to maximum by using it on the <col=800000>lava pool</col>. The "Heat-preform" option will increase the heat by small increments, while the "Dunk-preform" option will heat it faster. The temperature should be red.</col>
step	13	-	Quick guide step 13
line	<str>Minigame Teleport to "Giants' Foundry"</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac (strike the Hill Giant) in the Giants' Plateau.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once inside, repair the polishing wheel, grindstone, and trip hammer using the required items.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac twice.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate for items.</str>
line	
line	<str>Deposit all the items into the crucible (large bucket) hanging to the east by the bank. Different items are input separately.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac to learn how to select the moulds (in red text).</str>
line	
line	<str>Select the fitting mould Kovac described for the forte, blade and tip at the mould jig.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac again. He will tell you to pour the metal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pour the metal from the crucible into the mould.</str>
line	
line	<str>Get a bucket of water (grab a bucket from the pile of buckets and use it on the waterfall), and pour it on the sword. You can also use ice gloves for this step. Your hands must be free to pick up the preform.</str>
line	
line	<str>Heat the preform to maximum by using it on the lava pool. The "Heat-preform" option will increase the heat by small increments, while the "Dunk-preform" option will heat it faster. The temperature should be red.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Hit the preform with the Trip Hammer repaired earlier, repeating until progress bar is onto the yellow section. Be sure to keep the temperature in the red while doing this, otherwise the quality of the sword will decrease. Using the Trip Hammer will cool the preform.</col>
step	14	-	Quick guide step 14
line	<str>Minigame Teleport to "Giants' Foundry"</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac (strike the Hill Giant) in the Giants' Plateau.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once inside, repair the polishing wheel, grindstone, and trip hammer using the required items.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac twice.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate for items.</str>
line	
line	<str>Deposit all the items into the crucible (large bucket) hanging to the east by the bank. Different items are input separately.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac to learn how to select the moulds (in red text).</str>
line	
line	<str>Select the fitting mould Kovac described for the forte, blade and tip at the mould jig.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac again. He will tell you to pour the metal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pour the metal from the crucible into the mould.</str>
line	
line	<str>Get a bucket of water (grab a bucket from the pile of buckets and use it on the waterfall), and pour it on the sword. You can also use ice gloves for this step. Your hands must be free to pick up the preform.</str>
line	
line	<str>Heat the preform to maximum by using it on the lava pool. The "Heat-preform" option will increase the heat by small increments, while the "Dunk-preform" option will heat it faster. The temperature should be red.</str>
line	
line	<str>Hit the preform with the Trip Hammer repaired earlier, repeating until progress bar is onto the yellow section. Be sure to keep the temperature in the red while doing this, otherwise the quality of the sword will decrease. Using the Trip Hammer will cool the preform.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Cool the preform using the <col=800000>waterfall</col> until its temperature is almost green. The "Cool-preform" option will cool the preform slowly, while the "Quench-preform" option cools is more quickly.</col>
step	15	-	Quick guide step 15
line	<str>Minigame Teleport to "Giants' Foundry"</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac (strike the Hill Giant) in the Giants' Plateau.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once inside, repair the polishing wheel, grindstone, and trip hammer using the required items.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac twice.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate for items.</str>
line	
line	<str>Deposit all the items into the crucible (large bucket) hanging to the east by the bank. Different items are input separately.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac to learn how to select the moulds (in red text).</str>
line	
line	<str>Select the fitting mould Kovac described for the forte, blade and tip at the mould jig.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Kovac again. He will tell you to pour the metal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pour the metal from the crucible into the mould.</str>
line	
line	<str>Get a bucket of water (grab a bucket from the pile of buckets and use it on the waterfall), and pour it on the sword. You can also use ice gloves for this step. Your hands must be free to pick up the preform.</str>
line	
line	<str>Heat the preform to maximum by using it on the lava pool. The "Heat-preform" option will increase the heat by small increments, while the "Dunk-preform" option will heat it faster. The temperature should be red.</str>
line	
line	<str>Hit the preform with the Trip Hammer repaired earlier, repeating until progress bar is onto the yellow section. Be sure to keep the temperature in the red while doing this, otherwise the quality of the sword will decrease. Using the Trip Hammer will cool the preform.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cool the preform using the waterfall until its temperature is almost green. The "Cool-preform" option will cool the preform slowly, while the "Quench-preform" option cools is more quickly.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Use the preform on Grindstone repaired earlier, repeating until progress is onto green section. Be sure to watch the temperature as the Grindstone will heat the preform during use.</col>
